fix(transparency): cron upsert via delete+insert + render published chain on /transparency

The transparency-snapshot cron was returning written:0 because PostgREST's
`onConflict: "tenant_id,date"` couldn't resolve against the migration's
expression-based unique index (`coalesce(tenant_id::text,'')`). Switched
to an idempotent delete-then-insert path that handles both NULL-tenant
all-tenants rows and per-tenant rows with one code path.

/transparency public page now renders the chain:
- Reads transparency_roots WHERE tenant_id IS NULL — the all-tenants
  forensic chain we publish.
- Renders a compact 6-column table: UTC date · root_hex (first 32) ·
  AI runs · audit · cross-tenant · consent counts.
- Falls through gracefully if the table doesn't exist on a stale
  preview deploy.
- Per-tenant roots stay private to /app/trust + the JSON endpoint at
  /api/transparency/root/[date].

